N2  - This research applies systems engineering methodology to optimization of a CubeSat Test and Evaluation program. Currently, over 50% of CubeSats fail to perform their intended mission, in large part, due to inadequate test and evaluation procedures prior to flight. This paper applies Systems Engineering principles to increase the robustness and effectiveness of CubeSat test and evaluation with the goal of reducing the failure rate of CubeSat missions. This paper builds upon previous research to build the scalable systems architecture. The paper covers the set of model-based systems engineering diagrams and reports for the operational and logical/functional viewpoints of the CubeSat Test and Evaluation System.
AB  - This research applies systems engineering methodology to optimization of a CubeSat Test and Evaluation program. Currently, over 50% of CubeSats fail to perform their intended mission, in large part, due to inadequate test and evaluation procedures prior to flight. This paper applies Systems Engineering principles to increase the robustness and effectiveness of CubeSat test and evaluation with the goal of reducing the failure rate of CubeSat missions. This paper builds upon previous research to build the scalable systems architecture. The paper covers the set of model-based systems engineering diagrams and reports for the operational and logical/functional viewpoints of the CubeSat Test and Evaluation System.
